tests/isla/traces.sh traces every form from armv9p4-checked.ir, which this diff makes from
armv9p4.ir, the Armv9.4-A snapshot of the Sail model (isla-snapshots d8b31014).  Isla's harness
function isla_footprint_common (isla_main.sail 61-66) calls __DecodeA64 in a try block whose one
handler clears the exception and returns false, and the trace records nothing of the throw, so a
path on which the decoder throws SEE, UNDEFINED, or UNPREDICTABLE looks like a completed path.
Every exception entry of the model ends in EndOfInstruction, which throws Error_ExceptionTaken
(builtins.sail 52).  The edit keeps the handler for that exception and makes every other exception
fail a Sail assertion, which ends Isla's run with an error, so no trace that the script writes
holds a path that ended in another exception.  In Isla's IR, `x is C` holds when the constructor
of x differs from C (executor.rs 418-421 of Isla e9b5d945).  The edit inserts five statements, so
the jump that skips the handler moves from statement 32 to 37, the return.  With the permanently
undefined encoding UDF, the unedited IR gives a trace that looks complete, and the edited IR stops
with the assertion.  Apply with
`cp armv9p4.ir armv9p4-checked.ir && patch armv9p4-checked.ir < armv9p4-checked.diff`.

--- armv9p4.ir
+++ armv9p4-checked.ir
@@ -3771824,9 +3771824,14 @@
   goto 28;
   goto 29;
   zz40 = true `31 63:4-63:8;
-  jump @not(have_exception) goto 32 `31 61:2-66:3;
+  jump @not(have_exception) goto 37 `31 61:2-66:3;
   have_exception = false `31 61:2-66:3;
+  jump current_exception is zError_ExceptionTaken goto 34 `31 61:2-66:3;
   zz40 = false `31 65:9-65:14;
+  goto 37;
+  zz411 : %unit `31 61:2-66:3;
+  zz411 = zsail_assert(false, "__DecodeA64 threw an exception other than Error_ExceptionTaken") `31 61:2-66:3;
+  goto 37;
   return = zz40 `31 61:2-66:3;
   end;
 }
